WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:05.733
Your compliance team is one person.
The regulator’s expectations were written for fifty.

00:00:06.383 --> 00:00:12.285
Halima is the compliance officer at a
microfinance bank. She is also its money laundering

00:00:12.285 --> 00:00:15.667
reporting officer, and most
weeks its risk manager.

00:00:16.317 --> 00:00:20.400
In four years the bank grew from
three branches to nine, and added an app.

00:00:21.050 --> 00:00:26.973
Market traders deposit cash every evening.
Halima reviews it from spreadsheets exported on

00:00:26.973 --> 00:00:27.500
Fridays.

00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:33.388
The examiner asked a simple question: how
do you identify your higher-risk customers, and

00:00:33.388 --> 00:00:34.800
how do you monitor them?

00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:40.100
Halima knew the answer. She knew them by
sight. Almost none of it was written down.

00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:46.765
INFERIVA gives a microfinance bank the same
monitoring, screening and case records a large

00:00:46.765 --> 00:00:47.433
bank runs,

00:00:48.083 --> 00:00:53.622
with rules tuned to a cash-heavy book,
reporting thresholds set for its own jurisdiction,

00:00:53.622 --> 00:00:56.733
and pricing sized for
an institution of its scale.

00:00:57.383 --> 00:01:02.153
We begin with a quarter of your own
transactions: what the rules would have raised, and

00:01:02.153 --> 00:01:05.333
how much of it a small
team could clear in a working week.

00:01:05.983 --> 00:01:10.900
Halima’s judgement stays. It is simply on
the record, where an examiner can see it.

00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:17.914
Running compliance with a team of one or
two? Talk to INFERIVA about a set-up sized for

00:01:17.914 --> 00:01:18.133
it.
